\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces SLIC architecture (Condition~1 --- Full). Four entity token groups are encoded by dedicated linear layers. Intra-Set Self-Attention contextualises each entity set independently. Cross-Attention uses the self-embedding as query and each set as key/value. Red arrows highlight the role-conditioned routing path: the role one-hot in \texttt  {self\_tok} is projected into Q, while the role one-hots in \texttt  {ally\_tok} are projected into K/V, enabling structured role-pair attention routing without architectural hand-coding.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{8}{SLIC architecture (Condition~1 --- Full). Four entity token groups are encoded by dedicated linear layers. Intra-Set Self-Attention contextualises each entity set independently. Cross-Attention uses the self-embedding as query and each set as key/value. Red arrows highlight the role-conditioned routing path: the role one-hot in \texttt {self\_tok} is projected into Q, while the role one-hots in \texttt {ally\_tok} are projected into K/V, enabling structured role-pair attention routing without architectural hand-coding}{figure.1}{}}
